A||N||6||MR2KLR||3.1L help?||||1||
Z||000000||MR2KLR||11-18-2001||02:47 PM||||<BR>Since I have given up on a caddy V8 in my car I'm now looking at instaling a 3.1L V6 in place of the stock 2.5. I got from a friend (for free) a Holley 4-bbl intake for the 2.8/3.1 a Holley 700cfm carb and a plate NOS system (50-125 shot) My problem is what car do I get the 3.1 from? I searched the archive with no luck. every 3.1 I have found has been DIS. can a DIS 3.1 be changed over to a "Normal" setup? can any one help?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOYPICS/scrapbookFiles/importD3.gif"> <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A> <A HREF="mailto:Tomtom81@webtv.net">Tomtom81@webtv.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MR2KLR||11-18-2001||08:01 PM||||**Bump**<P>Anybody?||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT GT 87||11-18-2001||08:36 PM|||| With a carb. manifold you can use a regular distributer from a S-10  , it has a vacum advance  . Check out Taijiguy  He has a hot combo like what you want to do .||||reg||1
Z||000003||MR2KLR||11-18-2001||10:47 PM||||But where do I get a used long block from? all the ones I have found are Distributorless ing. system, there is a plug where the Distributor would go.<P>I guess what i'm asking is, What 3.1L FWD GM cars use a Distributor?<P>Thanks,<BR>   Tom||||reg||1
Z||000004||SKIDMARK||11-18-2001||11:16 PM||||If your intake manifold is for an older RWD 2.8, then it won't work on the aluminum head 3.1 from a FWD. The heads are totally different from the iron heads and in that case, you may want to consider an iron head 3.4 out of a Camaro. The 3.1 and 3.4 have a plug in the distrbutor hole but you can just remove it and install the Fiero 2.8 distributor. The stock intake for the 3.1 is in the way of the distributor. The 2.8, 3.1, and 3.4 all have the same basic block design but the 3.4 is reinforced and thicker. <BR>Since yours is a 2.5, you will need the V-6 electronics, wiring harness, some of the plumbing, and accessory brackets. If your going to go that far, get some info on just installing the FWD 3.1 wiring harness, computer and all and forget about your carb and manifold. I've found that usually free things like that end up costing a lot of money and time. That's probably why the guy gave them to you! Good luck with your project.||||reg||1
Z||000005||MR2KLR||11-19-2001||07:48 AM||||Thanks for the info "SKIDMARK" the intake manifold if for a early 2.8L like 83-88) s10 that did not have alu. heads and is made by Edelbrock.  <P>Thanks,<BR> Tom||||reg||1
Z||000006||MR2KLR||11-19-2001||07:51 AM|||| What heads are on a older 82-8x 2.8L Camaro? are they HO 2.8 heads like the fiero? Is there a 4-bbl intake that will work on a 3.1L Motor? Will the stock 3.1 Cam work?<p>[This message has been edited by MR2KLR (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
